meta {
  name: AI Re-run on Video Post (asserts AI_EXTRACTION_FAILED in mock mode)
  type: http
  seq: 15
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{videoPostId}}/video/ai-rerun
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 502
}

tests {
  test("response carries AI_EXTRACTION_FAILED code", function() {
    expect(res.body.code).to.equal("AI_EXTRACTION_FAILED");
  });
}

docs {
  Owner-only re-extraction at POST /:id/video/ai-rerun. The route's
  preconditions are all satisfied (owner = testuser, video.status =
  'ready', transcript present), so the request reaches the
  `runExtractVideoMetadata` call inside the advisory-locked transaction.

  ── Why this asserts 502 instead of 200 ──────────────────────────────
  The seeded mock-script for video-metadata
  (packages/server/src/plugins/langchain/mock-scripts.ts) emits chunks
  whose concatenation is `{...valid JSON...}[done]`. The chain wraps
  the model in StringOutputParser, returning the raw concatenated
  string verbatim. `runExtractVideoMetadata`'s `tryParseAttempt`
  then calls `JSON.parse(raw)` directly — the trailing `[done]`
  sentinel causes a SyntaxError, the retry hits the same bug, and
  the route surfaces `AiExtractionFailedError` as a 502 with
  `code: 'AI_EXTRACTION_FAILED'`.

  This is a pre-existing bug in the mock path (the production path
  with a real LLM returns clean JSON and works). Fixing it requires
  either stripping `/\[done\]$/` inside `streamAndAccumulate` or
  removing the `[done]` chunk from the videoMetadata mock script —
  both server-code changes that are out of WU7b's scope.

  Asserting 502 + AI_EXTRACTION_FAILED here pins the CURRENT runtime
  behavior so a future fix (when it lands) intentionally inverts this
  assertion — preventing silent regressions in either direction. When
  the mock-mode bug is fixed, update the assertion to:
    res.status: eq 200
    body has { runId, title, description, tags }
  and remove this docs block.
}
